      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I get the frustration — cramps wrecking your sleep is miserable, and \"I'll just call them Monday\" feels like a lifetime when you're hurting tonight.\n\nBut no, don't take the extra-strength potassium pill. \"I feel fine\" is exactly how hyperkalemia works — it's often silent until it isn't, and the first symptom can be a heart rhythm problem, not a warning twinge. One high-dose pill on top of lisinopril is a real risk, not a theoretical one.\n\n**For tonight, try this instead:** stretch your calves before bed, stay hydrated, and a warm shower or a bit of magnesium-rich food (nuts, spinach) is a safer bet. And honestly, mention the cramps when you call — they're a known lisinopril side effect, and your doctor might tweak your dose or timing rather than have you self-treat.",
